1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,833
Dad, why do you have hair down there? And in your armpits too!

2
00:00:03,833 --> 00:00:08,033
That's… because grown-ups get cold down there! It's a fur blanket!

3
00:00:08,033 --> 00:00:09,500
It's not a blanket.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:10,400
…Huh?

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:13,500
Wrong answer number one. I'm Modapman.

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,433
Case summary. Next day, the neighborhood barbershop. My kid told him everything.

7
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:22,700
He's been asking the whole neighborhood since this morning.

8
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:26,100
If it's about hair, you came to the right place. I've cut it for fifty years.

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,733
Shave it and it grows back thicker. So don't go shaving.

10
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:34,767
It doesn't. The cut tip is blunt, so it just feels thicker.

11
00:00:34,767 --> 00:00:38,833
Wrong answer, two. Mom, the model answer… usually.

12
00:00:38,867 --> 00:00:42,333
But Grandpa, why is there no hair on your head, but lots on your chest?

13
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:46,033
That's because he used his head so much, the hair wore off!

14
00:00:46,033 --> 00:00:49,867
Smart people go bald! My thin front is proof of all my studying.

15
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:51,700
I never studied.

16
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:54,933
Wrong answer, three. Not proof of studying.

17
00:00:54,967 --> 00:00:58,067
Before I pick up the scissors, let's do just three rounds.

18
00:00:58,067 --> 00:00:59,300
A haircut has rounds…?

19
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:02,367
Round one. Hair doesn't sprout out of nowhere.

20
00:01:02,367 --> 00:01:06,567
Fine fuzz is already all over your body. Even on this kid's arm.

21
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:08,133
Huh? It's really there!

22
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:11,333
When the time comes, your body sends a 'getting ready to grow up' signal.

23
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:18,033
Then the fuzz on the chin, the sideburns, the armpits and down there turns into thick hair.

24
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:19,767
Ah, puberty!

25
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:23,500
Round two. Why the armpits and down there, of all places?

26
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:28,200
Those spots have a special sweat gland. It sweats right into the hair root.

27
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,700
Sweat into the hair?

28
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:33,767
The hair is a wick that holds that sweat. Like a candle wick.

29
00:01:33,767 --> 00:01:38,700
And the smell isn't the sweat. The bacteria living on the skin make it.

30
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:41,767
So that's why armpits start to smell as kids grow up.

31
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:45,067
That gland switches on with the same signal.

32
00:01:45,067 --> 00:01:47,300
Round three. My head.

33
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:51,967
Same signal, but the hair on top of the head hears it backwards.

34
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:57,633
To the beard and chest it says 'get thick.' To the top of the head, 'get thin.'

35
00:01:57,633 --> 00:02:00,867
Oh, so the head hair moved down to the chest!

36
00:02:00,867 --> 00:02:04,833
It didn't move. Different hairs just hear it differently.

37
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:08,367
The sides and back don't react, so a horseshoe is left.

38
00:02:08,367 --> 00:02:10,667
So that's why your hair is shaped like a U?

39
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:15,533
Yep. That's why if you move hair from the back to the front, it stays.

40
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:21,233
In one line: fuzz gets thick, glands switch on, and only the top of the head goes the other way.

41
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:24,933
What I said yesterday wasn't a real answer. Sorry.

42
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:30,233
You've got hair all over too. When you grow up, a few spots will get thicker.

43
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:34,000
It's not dirty, and it's not embarrassing. It's just growing up.

44
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,067
Then when will mine?

45
00:02:36,067 --> 00:02:39,467
Your body knows. Ask me anytime you're curious.

46
00:02:39,467 --> 00:02:43,767
But when it's about someone else's body, use a quiet voice. Promise?

47
00:02:43,767 --> 00:02:48,133
Promise. …Grandpa, sorry I said it so loudly.

48
00:02:48,133 --> 00:02:52,667
It's alright. My head has been my pride for fifty years.

49
00:02:52,767 --> 00:02:54,800
Will you go bald too, Dad?

50
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:59,367
Don't worry! Baldness comes from Mom's side, they say. Her dad has plenty of hair!

51
00:02:59,367 --> 00:03:01,533
Only half right. You take after your dad's side too.

52
00:03:01,533 --> 00:03:04,333
But your dad, Grandpa… is super shiny.

53
00:03:04,333 --> 00:03:06,033
…We'll be late for dinner. Let's go.

54
00:03:06,033 --> 00:03:09,333
Wrong answer, four. Modapman strikes again.
